# Copy this file to .env and adjust as needed.
# Local Ollama (default, free):
OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
OPENAI_API_KEY=ollama
# The derived model pins num_ctx to 16384. The stock llama3.2 declares a
# 131072 token context but Ollama allocates about 4096 at load time when no
# num_ctx is set, and it truncates the FRONT of an oversized prompt without
# reporting anything. Build it with: ollama create llama3.2-ctx16k -f Modelfile
# Verify with: python probe_context.py
OPENAI_MODEL=llama3.2-ctx16k
# Whisper model size for the audio module (tiny, base, small, medium)
WHISPER_MODEL=base

# Vision-language model for slide-image extraction (the third model, image
# data). Any Ollama VLM works; swap it here with no code change. Pull it with:
# ollama pull qwen2.5vl:7b
VISION_MODEL=qwen2.5vl:7b
# Slide rendering for the vision path (defaults shown). The page cap is a
# safety limit only and sits above the length of a real lecture deck:
# VISION_DPI=150
# VISION_MAX_PAGES=200

# --- Per-slide routing ---
# The interface offers per-slide routing first: a slide goes to the vision
# model only when pictures cover at least 10 per cent of it (PowerPoint), or
# when its text layer holds fewer than 60 words (PDF). The thresholds were
# derived by measurement and live in modules/slide_routing.py. Override them
# here only for an experiment:
# SLIDE_ROUTING_PICTURE_THRESHOLD=0.10
# SLIDE_ROUTING_WORDS_THRESHOLD=60

# --- Reproducibility controls (both unset by default) ---
# When unset they are NOT sent to the model, which reproduces the exact
# behaviour evaluated in the Preliminary Project Report. Set them to make a
# run repeatable, e.g. for separating an input-mode effect from sampling
# noise in the evaluation:
# LLM_TEMPERATURE=0
# LLM_SEED=42

# Request timeout in seconds for a single model call. Defaults to 600 (the
# OpenAI client's own default), so leaving it unset changes nothing:
# LLM_TIMEOUT=600

# --- Long-input handling (unset by default) ---
# Optional per-source word cap for the prompt context. Unset means no limit
# (today's behaviour). When set, each source is truncated to at most this
# many words and the truncation is reported on screen and in the saved file:
# MAX_CONTEXT_WORDS=4000

# --- Quiz format validation ---
# Validation always runs and is recorded in the saved output. Retry is off by
# default (1 attempt = today's behaviour). Raise it to regenerate a quiz that
# fails validation, using the identical unchanged prompt:
# QUIZ_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3

# --- Structured quiz generation ---
# The interface generates the quiz under a JSON schema, so it always returns
# five questions and each names a source that was supplied. It can be
# switched off in the sidebar. The batch runner (evaluation/run_eval.py) uses
# the original prompt-only path unless this is set to 1, so that it keeps
# reproducing the reference condition. Setting it to 0 also starts the
# interface on the original path:
# QUIZ_STRUCTURED=1
